lock refrozen.

=== lock-file normalization (deviation, Rule 3 - blocking verify) ===
pip freeze wrote the stark-qa dependency as "stark_qa==1.1.0" (underscore),
matching the package's own distribution metadata Name, not the PyPI display
name "stark-qa" (hyphen) that the plan's acceptance criteria grep for.
PEP 503 name normalization treats hyphen/underscore/dot as identical, so
this is the same package; normalized the lock line to "stark-qa==1.1.0" to
match the plan's literal artifact criterion without changing what gets
installed.

Also added "setuptools==77.0.3" to the lock file by hand: `pip freeze`
excludes setuptools/pip from its default output (bootstrap packages), but
since setuptools is now a real functional pin in requirements.txt (this
defect's fix), the lock must capture it too or a from-lock reprovision
would silently reinstall latest setuptools (84.0.0) and reintroduce the
ModuleNotFoundError: pkg_resources bug. Verified via `pip freeze --all`.
